@* Ported from legacy Content/PrivacyPolicyContent.html; the wording is VETQAS's and is kept as written. *@
<h1 class="govuk-heading-l">VETQAS privacy notice</h1>

<p class="govuk-body">
    This privacy notice explains how personal data is used, stored, and processed by VETQAS. If you have any queries about the
    content of this privacy notice, please email <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:vetqas@apha.gov.uk">vetqas@apha.gov.uk</a>.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Who collects your personal data?</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (Defra) is the controller for the personal data we collect:
</p>
<address class="govuk-body">
    Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs<br>
    Seacole Building<br>
    2 Marsham Street<br>
    London<br>
    SW1P 4DF
</address>
<p class="govuk-body">
    If you need further information about how Defra uses your personal data and your associated rights, you can contact the Defra
    data protection manager at
    <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:data.protection@defra.gov.uk">data.protection@defra.gov.uk</a> or at the above address.
</p>
<p class="govuk-body">
    The data protection officer for Defra is responsible for checking that Defra complies with legislation. You can contact them at
    <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:DefraGroupDataProtectionOfficer@defra.gov.uk">DefraGroupDataProtectionOfficer@defra.gov.uk</a>
    or at the above address.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What personal data we collect and process</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">We collect your:</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>Name</li>
    <li>Contact details</li>
    <li>Role (e.g. customer, test commentator)</li>
</ul>

<p class="govuk-body">
    We use this data for the following purposes, depending on your role associated with VETQAS:
</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>Customer contracts and invoicing</li>
    <li>Test Report commentating</li>
    <li>Report Viewing</li>
    <li>Mailing list</li>
    <li>Market surveys</li>
    <li>Regulatory compliance (in specific cases of disease monitoring)</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Lawful basis for processing your personal data</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">The lawful basis for processing your personal data is:</p>
<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>Contractual – It is necessary for the performance of a commercial contract with VETQAS to provide you with Proficiency Testing services.</li>
    <li>Legal Obligations - In some cases, for compliance with an obligation for disease surveillance and/or veterinary surveillance purposes. Examples include tuberculosis, poultry health, TSEs, and BSE.</li>
</ol>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Consent to process your personal data</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">The processing of your personal data is not based on consent. You cannot withdraw it.</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Who we share your personal data with</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    We may share the personal data collected under this privacy notice with:
</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>
        British Equine Veterinary Association (BEVA) – if you are registered under their scheme for the testing of CEMO, Klebsiella
        pneumoniae, and Pseudomonas aeruginosa. More information is available
        <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.beva.org.uk/Vets/BEVA-Registered-Lab-Scheme" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">on the BEVA registered lab scheme page (opens in new tab)</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
        Poultry Health Scheme (PHS) – if you are a member of the Poultry Health Scheme. More information is available
        <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/poultry-health-scheme-how-to-register" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">in the Poultry Health Scheme guidance (opens in new tab)</a>.
    </li>
</ul>
<p class="govuk-body">
    We respect your personal privacy when responding to access to information requests. We only share information when necessary to
    meet the statutory requirements of the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 and the Freedom of Information Act 2000.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">How long we hold personal data</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    We will keep your personal data for 7 years from the date of the last Proficiency Testing Scheme with which you were involved.
    In line with health surveillance requirements, limited data associated with TSE and BSE testing is retained for 20 years and 50
    years after the testing date, respectively.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What happens if you do not provide the personal data?</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    If you do not provide the personal data, we will not be able to enrol you in any Proficiency Testing Schemes or provide you with
    data from the Schemes.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Use of automated decision-making or profiling</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">The personal data you provide is not used for:</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>Automated decision making (deciding by automated means without any human involvement)</li>
    <li>Profiling (automated processing of personal data to evaluate certain things about an individual)</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Your rights</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">Based on the lawful processing above, your individual rights are:</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>The right to be informed</li>
    <li>The right to rectification</li>
    <li>The right to erasure</li>
    <li>The right of access</li>
    <li>The right to restrict processing</li>
    <li>Rights in relation to automated decision making and profiling</li>
</ul>
<p class="govuk-body">
    More information about your individual rights under the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection
    Act 2018 (DPA 2018) can be found
    <a class="govuk-link" href="https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/uk-gdpr-guidance-and-resources/individual-rights/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">on the ICO website (opens in new tab)</a>.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Complaints</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    You have the right to
    <a class="govuk-link" href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">make a complaint (opens in new tab)</a>
    to the Information Commissioner’s Office at any time.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Personal information charter</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    Our
    <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/department-for-environment-food-rural-affairs/about/personal-information-charter" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">personal information charter (opens in new tab)</a>
    explains more about your rights over your personal data.
</p>
